          alt: "Airway procedures — size it, time it, watch the patient. Oropharyngeal airway: size from the incisors to the angle of the jaw; too long presses the epiglottis shut, too short pushes the tongue back; only if the gag reflex is absent — in a patient who still has a gag it provokes vomiting, and if she resists it she does not need it. Suction: pre-oxygenate, insert with no suction applied, apply only on withdrawal, ten to fifteen seconds at most, then let the patient recover; suction removes oxygen along with secretions. At every tracheostomy bedside: two spare tubes, dilators, tested suction, saline and syringe.",
